  "actor": "HARNESS",
  "what": "problem PD-1@v2 drafted",
  "phase": "DEFINE",
  "minute": 116.0,
  "event_seq": 270,
  "root_problem": "Dispute ticket volume nearly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul) to ~1180-1260/month (Aug-Sep) (E-05). For the ESTIMATED-read portion of disputed bills (1240 of 3025, E-02), AMI read-event data shows 1184 had a valid, timely read nonetheless rejected as REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION (E-11). This is caused by validation rule BV-17 (deployed 2026-08-01) comparing the raw AMI register value directly against 12-month m3 history with unit_scaling=none (E-12), while firmware v4.2 meters (rolled out 2026-06) report register values in units of 0.1 m3 rather than m3 (E-13) — making normal v4.2 readings appear ~10x inflated and triggering unwarranted high-consumption rejection and forced estimate substitution. This confirmed mechanism (H-HIGHCONSUMPTION-REJECT, H-BV17-UNIT-SCALE-BUG) accounts for the 1184/1240 ESTIMATED-read dispute subset; it does not explain the larger 1785-of-3025 ACTUAL-read dispute majority (E-02), whose cause is still unknown."
 },
